## Claim
Text: "The iPhone 12 won’t come with earphones and a charging adapter."
Claim date: October 14, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Apple officially announce on or before October 14, 2020, that the iPhone 12 would not include earphones in the retail box?
Answer: The search result does not contain any indication that Apple officially announced, on or before October 14, 2020, that the iPhone 12 would not include earphones. It only reports predictions from an analyst and notes that Apple did not respond to a request for comment. Therefore, based on this source, there is no evidence of an official announcement.

Source URL: https://www.cnet.com/tech/mobile/iphone-12-will-likely-come-sans-earbuds-and-power-adapter/

### Did Apple officially announce on or before October 14, 2020, that the iPhone 12 would not include a charging adapter in the retail box?
Answer: Yes, Apple officially announced on October 14, 2020, that the iPhone 12 series would not include a charging adapter in the box. The source states: "Apple has announced that the iPhone 12 series smartphones, which were unveiled today, won’t come bundled with a charging adapter in the box."

Source URL: https://ijunkie.com/iphone-12-does-not-ship-charger-earphones-in-box/

### Did the iPhone 12 retail box, when it became available to consumers, contain any earphones (wired or wireless)?
Answer: No, the iPhone 12 retail box did not contain any earphones (wired or wireless). The source explicitly states that "they don't ship with EarPods" and that "iPhone 12 and iPhone 12 mini do not include a power adapter or EarPods."

Source URL: https://wccftech.com/apple-iphone-12-mini-and-iphone-12-pro-max-retail-box-contents/

### Did the iPhone 12 retail box, when it became available to consumers, contain a charging adapter (power brick)?
Answer: Yes, the iPhone 12 retail box did not contain a charging adapter (power brick) when it became available to consumers. The article confirms that "Apple will no longer include those items in the box," specifically noting that "the standard outlet adapter for the power cable" is omitted.

Source URL: https://techcrunch.com/2020/10/13/iphones-wont-come-with-headphones-or-power-adapters-in-the-box-from-now-on/

### Did the iPhone 12 retail box include a USB‑C to Lightning cable as the only included accessory?
Answer: Yes, according to the source, the iPhone 12 retail box included only the phone and a USB‑C to Lightning cable, with no other accessories such as EarPods or a power adapter. The article states: "iPhone 12 Mini and iPhone 12 Pro Max Retail Contents Feature Just the Phone itself and a USB-C to Lightning Cable."

Source URL: https://wccftech.com/apple-iphone-12-mini-and-iphone-12-pro-max-retail-box-contents/

### Did Apple provide a specific reason (e.g., environmental goals) for removing earphones and the charging adapter from the iPhone 12 box?
Answer: The search result does not contain a direct statement from Apple providing a specific reason for removing earphones and the charging adapter from the iPhone 12 box. It speculates that environmental goals may be a factor, citing Apple's statement about the Apple Watch Series 6, but no official reason for the iPhone 12 is given.

Source URL: https://www.mensxp.com/technology/hacks/81011-iphone-12-box-wont-have-earphones.html

### Did previous iPhone models (e.g., iPhone 11) include both earphones and a charging adapter in the box?
Answer: Yes, previous iPhone models like the iPhone 11 included both earphones (the familiar white Lightning headphones) and a charging adapter (the standard outlet adapter) in the box. The article confirms that Apple "will no longer include those items" starting with the iPhone 12, implying they were included before.

Source URL: https://techcrunch.com/2020/10/13/iphones-wont-come-with-headphones-or-power-adapters-in-the-box-from-now-on/

### Was the removal of earphones and the charging adapter confirmed by Apple’s product page or press release for the iPhone 12?
Answer: Yes, the removal of earphones and the charging adapter was confirmed by Apple’s product page. The search result quotes Apple’s website stating: “As part of our efforts to reach our environmental goals, iPhone 12 and iPhone 12 mini do not include a power adapter or EarPods,” with a similar message for the Pro models. This serves as official confirmation from Apple.

Source URL: https://www.macrumors.com/2020/10/13/iphone-12-ships-without-earpods-or-charger/

### Did any reliable news reports or leaks before October 14, 2020, state that the iPhone 12 would ship without earphones and a charging adapter?
Answer: Yes, the Tom's Guide article (published before October 14, 2020) reports that a leaker on Twitter (@L0vetodream) stated on July 1, 2020: "in my dream, the new IPhone will not come with the charger and earphone," and the article notes that "multiple analysts" had also reported the same. This constitutes a reliable news report and leak prior to the claim date.

Source URL: https://www.tomsguide.com/news/iphone-12-confirmed-to-ship-without-charger-but-at-least-the-box-will-be-nice

### Did the iPhone 12 packaging include any alternative accessories (e.g., a SIM eject tool, stickers, documentation) that replaced the earphones and charging adapter?
Answer: The search result does not contain sufficient information to answer the question about alternative accessories such as a SIM eject tool, stickers, or documentation in the iPhone 12 packaging. It only mentions that a Lightning to USB-C cable is expected to be included, but no other accessories are specified.

Source URL: https://www.macrumors.com/2020/06/28/kuo-no-charger-in-iphone-12-box/

## Final Judgement
The fact-check evidence consistently confirms that Apple officially announced on October 14, 2020, that the iPhone 12 would not include a charging adapter, and multiple sources (including Apple’s own product page) state that neither EarPods nor a power adapter are included in the box. The retail box contents are reported to contain only the phone and a USB‑C to Lightning cable, with no earphones or charging adapter. No evidence contradicts this. Therefore, the claim is fully supported.

